KNOWNBUG gcc16
main.cpp
--cpp11 --unwind 2 --depth 200 --no-unwinding-assertions --no-built-in-assertions
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
GCC 16's std::list implementation uses __allocated_obj RAII
guards that cause symex to explore exponentially many paths.
The --depth limit prevents the blowup but is a workaround.
